Backport of https://github.com/bootc-dev/bootc/pull/2661 ("Support bcachefs
in filesystem installs and updates"), applied on top of v1.17.5.

The PR cherry-picks onto v1.17.5 with no conflicts. It supersedes our earlier
hand-written 0001-add-bcachefs-filesystem-support.patch: it covers the same
Filesystem::Bcachefs plumbing (mkfs.bcachefs via the -U arm, enum, TryFrom,
man page), and additionally:

  - rejects a bcachefs root without a separate /boot *before* --wipe, so a
    request GRUB cannot boot no longer destroys the target disk first
  - resolves multi-device roots (bcachefs reports a colon-separated source,
    /dev/vda:/dev/vdb, which the old single-device path choked on)
  - recovers fs UUID/label from blkid when udev is unavailable

Note bcachefs does not implement fs-verity, so composefs installs onto it
still need --allow-missing-verity; that is unchanged by this PR and tracked
in https://github.com/bootc-dev/bootc/issues/2341

Delete this file entirely once the PR is merged and a release containing it
is what we build against.

